L["Plateau replaces the way enemy nameplates look: the health bar, name, cast bar, auras and icons. Everything is drawn by Plateau, but the game still decides what is shown, so it keeps working in dungeons and raids.\n\nThis window has three parts. The preview at the top shows a sample nameplate that updates as you change things. The menu on the left lists a page for each part of the nameplate, grouped by what they do. The page on the right holds that part's settings.\n\nEvery change saves right away. There is no Apply or Save button. Settings live in a profile: each character has a default profile, and the active profile is the one you are editing."] = "Plateau replaces the way enemy nameplates look: the health bar, name, cast bar, auras and icons. Everything is drawn by Plateau, but the game still decides what is shown, so it keeps working in dungeons and raids.\n\nThis window has three parts. The preview at the top shows a sample nameplate that updates as you change things. The menu on the left lists a page for each part of the nameplate, grouped by what they do. The page on the right holds that part's settings.\n\nEvery change saves right away. There is no Apply or Save button. Settings live in a profile: each character has a default profile, and the active profile is the one you are editing."
