L["Style friendly nameplates with Plateau decides whether friendly players and NPCs use Plateau's look, with its own scale and an option to hide them in combat. In dungeons, raids and arenas the game locks friendly nameplates, so Blizzard draws them there and Blizzard's friendly nameplates, at the bottom of the page, apply instead. Blizzard nameplate size is Blizzard's own Nameplate Size, the same setting as Nameplate size on the Size page, so it sizes friendly players there too.\n\nFriendly nameplates at the top holds what players and NPCs share: scale, names only, name offset and the guild and title text size. Friendly players holds everything for players: their switch, name size, class and name colors, guild names and realm names; Hide realm marker (*) takes effect after a /reload. Friendly NPCs holds the same for NPCs, including Show NPC titles. Guild names and NPC titles need Show names only. Pets and minions has one switch for the open world, where Plateau draws friendly nameplates, and one for dungeons and raids, where the game draws them. Raid target icon lets friendly nameplates place the raid icon on their own."] = "Style friendly nameplates with Plateau decides whether friendly players and NPCs use Plateau's look, with its own scale and an option to hide them in combat. In dungeons, raids and arenas the game locks friendly nameplates, so Blizzard draws them there and Blizzard's friendly nameplates, at the bottom of the page, apply instead. Blizzard nameplate size is Blizzard's own Nameplate Size, the same setting as Nameplate size on the Size page, so it sizes friendly players there too.\n\nFriendly nameplates at the top holds what players and NPCs share: scale, names only, name offset and the guild and title text size. Friendly players holds everything for players: their switch, name size, class and name colors, guild names and realm names; Hide realm marker (*) takes effect after a /reload. Friendly NPCs holds the same for NPCs, including Show NPC titles. Guild names and NPC titles need Show names only. Pets and minions has one switch for the open world, where Plateau draws friendly nameplates, and one for dungeons and raids, where the game draws them. Raid target icon lets friendly nameplates place the raid icon on their own."
